    "q-182489": {
      "dom_id": "step-q182489",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "If $A$ is false and $B$ is true, then $A⇒B$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The statement $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. \n\nSo, when $A=\\text{F}$ and $B=\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A⇒B) & ≡(\\text{F}⇒\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete truth table for $A⇒B$ is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A⇒B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "select",
          "dom_id": "selectList-182489-0",
          "tag": "custom-select",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "0",
              "dom_id": null,
              "type": "text",
              "value": "always false",
              "html": "always false"
            },
            {
              "option": "1",
              "dom_id": null,
              "type": "text",
              "value": "sometimes true",
              "html": "sometimes true"
            },
            {
              "option": "2",
              "dom_id": null,
              "type": "text",
              "value": "sometimes false",
              "html": "sometimes false"
            },
            {
              "option": "3",
              "dom_id": null,
              "type": "text",
              "value": "always true",
              "html": "always true"
            }
          ],
          "dom_index": 0,
          "disabled": false,
